Z||000000||ponya||07-11-2000||09:29 PM||||Anyone know where a person could get a copy of this manual. Having the part numbers would be invaluable. Found the publisher of the P22 manual for the Fiero, but it is no longer published. Any other sources of part numbers out there? Any info appreciated. Thanks,<BR>Bob||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-11-2000||10:13 PM||||Bob, Try clicking the e-bay link at the bottom of the page. Every once in a while, someone will have a 22P book for sale. They usually are not too cheap, though.<P>------------------<BR>-------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-11-2000||10:27 PM||||Bob, there is a guy up in Michigan who has tons of manuals (not all P-22's) of all kinds -- I have bought from him before. I'll look for his info and get it to ya as soon as i can. And, Raydar is right, they aren't cheap!! nothing out of print is, right?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||07-11-2000||10:59 PM||||If you do a lot of your own work it's useful not just because of the complete parts list, the back half of the book is exploded diagrams showing the components of the assemblies and how they fit together, most of these schematics aren't in any of the shop manuals, even the Helms.   <P>The going rate on Ebay of an unused and clear-wrapped November 90 version (last version printed) of the manual right now seems to be about $50. <p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||HarryG||07-12-2000||12:40 PM||||If you can't find a paper copy, I think someone on one of the other lists mentioned they had found a source for the P22 on microfiche.  Price was reasonable; I think the source was Bell & Howell.||||reg||1
Z||000005||HarryG||07-21-2000||12:31 PM||||Bob,<BR>If you haven't located a hard copy yet, I finally found my Bell & Howell info. The 22P on microfiche costs $6.00 plus tax. Call 800/221-5362 ext. 4186 to get an order form.<BR>Harry  ||||reg||3
Z||000006||terryk||07-21-2000||03:13 PM||||Wait, on Ebay you can get them for 10 times that price.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||07-21-2000||08:47 PM||||I was e-mailing bidders at e-bay to let them know they were being raked for $24.00 dollars for the microfiche and let them know about B/H! Just like looking out for other Fiero owners <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> The fiche aren't much good to anyone without a reader though and I soon discovered it takes mega hours to make a complete copy from the fiche. I gave up after 20 pages and finally broke down and bought the manual <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||HarryG||07-22-2000||09:43 AM||||Most libraries have microfiche readers you could use.  Sometimes you can buy them at school/govt. auctions. But I agree, getting the fiche to make a complete paper copy would not be the way to go.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ponya||07-22-2000||03:54 PM||||Just wanted to say Thanks to everyone for all their suggestions. I finally got a copy from ebay. Paid $ 6l.00, a lot of money, but I think it will pay off in the long run. Again, thanks to all.  Bob||||reg||6
